# Code Conventions

## No console output in `src/`

Engine code ships inside the artifact a planner runs. `console.log` / `debug` / `info` are
banned in `src/` (enforced by suite D9). Five leftover debug statements in `hc-search.ts`
were removed for this reason. If you need visibility during development, use the test
suites, not logging in shipped code. `console.warn`/`console.error` for genuine
user-facing faults are acceptable — debug tracing is not.

## Never duplicate an algorithm

`searchOptimalHC` and `searchOptimalHCAsync` are ~500 lines of near-identical logic. They
have already drifted: the sync version silently rewrites `sla.clockStartPolicy` when >15%
of volume arrives off-hours, and the async version — **which is the one the UI actually
calls** (`App.tsx`) — does not. The same input can therefore size differently depending on
the entry point.

Do not add a third copy, and do not fix a bug in one without the other. The correct
resolution is one shared implementation that the async variant wraps with progress
callbacks and yields.

The same hazard exists between `CaseMinHeap.compare` (used by the real dispatch loop) and
`pickNextCase`/`compareByUrgency` (used only by the test harnesses). Two orderings that can
diverge means the harness may validate behaviour that does not ship.

## All time math goes through `calendar.ts`

Never hand-roll `Date` arithmetic in engine code. Business-hours math is subtle — holidays,
weekends, daily open/close, half-open horizon boundaries — and it is centralised in
`src/utils/calendar.ts` for exactly that reason. Use `addWorkingTime`,
`subtractWorkingTime`, `workingDuration`, `isWorking`, `nextOpen`,
`getCalendarWorkingDaysInHorizon`.

Note `getCalendarWorkingDaysInHorizon` treats the horizon as **half-open** `[start, end)`.
An inclusive bound counts a trailing zero-demand day whenever `horizonEnd` lands exactly on
midnight — which happens for whole-day interval data and *always* for 24x7 calendars.

## Round only at the presentation boundary

Keep full precision through the calculation chain; round when producing output for display
or for a stored result field. Rounding mid-chain compounds. Compare floats with a tolerance
(`Math.abs(a - b) <= tol`), never `===`.

## Determinism

The engine must be reproducible for a given seed. Anything that introduces
run-to-run variance breaks the CI-gated search:
- `Map`/`Set` iteration order depends on insertion order — sort explicitly when order
  affects a result (e.g. `allocateAgentsToCategories` sorts category names for
  deterministic tie-breaking).
- Never use `Math.random()`. Use the seeded `createPrng` in `des-engine.ts`.
- Never use `Date.now()` or `new Date()` for anything that affects a computed result.
